    "references": [
     {
      "id": "boretzky1994romani",
      "short": "B1994a",
      "source": "Norbert Boretzky and Birgit Igla\\.\n*Wörterbuch Romani\\-Deutsch\\-Englisch für den südosteuropäischen Raum: Mit einer Grammatik der Dialektvarianten*\\.\nHarrassowitz, Wiesbaden, 1994\\.\nISBN 9783447034593\\.\nThe appendix deliberately covers “alte Etyma aus allen Dialekten” of European Romani rather than only the southeastern varieties of the dictionary proper, and cites every word in the shape it carries as a main entry there\\. The scanned copy lacks the volume's front matter, so its abbreviation key and transcription description were not available; the source abbreviations used in the lists were resolved from the printed Literaturverzeichnis\\.",
      "progress": "The etymological appendix “Etymologien” on printed pages 311--338 only, i.e. its four alphabetical word lists: Indische Etyma (pp. 311--328), Iranische Etyma (pp. 329--331), Armenische Etyma (pp. 331--332) and Griechische Etyma (pp. 333--338). Every printed entry in those lists is represented. Excludes the A--Z Romani-German-English dictionary (pp. 1--310), the German-Romani and English-Romani reverse indexes (pp. 339--362), the Variantengrammatik (pp. 363--417) and the Literaturverzeichnis (pp. 417--418). The “s. X” cross-reference lines inside the lists are pointers to a full entry elsewhere in the same appendix and are recorded in the audit rather than installed as forms",
      "provenance": "Copyrighted Harrassowitz volume, not redistributed; scanned PDF SHA-256 2fc3678f13736e2c9f2f857a123803efde6955e56f2ad53ce4d3cb184771d6ee, 425 page images, no text layer. Hand-collated transcription layer in data/other/forms/raw_data/20260825-boretzky-igla-etymologies-extract.psv; importer data/other/forms/raw_data/boretzky_igla_1994.py; per-record audit data/other/forms/raw_data/20260825-boretzky-igla-etymologies-audit.csv and seeded sample data/other/forms/raw_data/20260825-boretzky-igla-etymologies-sample.csv; installed rows data/other/forms/20260825-boretzky-igla-etymologies.csv",
      "editor": "Aryaman Arora and Anthropic Claude",
